{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"412947d04be4ac4760897ea79a7501391496bb7127c6013efd8db440380b34cd","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_9c2726f5e2a49e576c95021bdf1d6f812c107c0468fc696e1eddfe8a16a8d41f","overall_assessment":"Doc2VecC presents a significant contribution to document representation learning by offering a highly efficient and effective alternative to existing state-of-the-art methods. Its simplicity, scalability, and strong performance across multiple tasks make it a valuable tool for both researchers and practitioners, with clear practical benefits in terms of computational cost and ease of deployment.","paper_id":"B1Igu2ogg","paper_identity_sha256":"afd93b966d20e4861e4f5cf45c43d42bf44c7dcfb3e6929638f2944bfcf5d591","prompt_identity_sha256":"df785441fa120e465eb4a239fdc07928b9dc68cf02b4e69378c11bd9001191a6","raw_response_sha256":"016086e204a01334fa8a3fad7a05be3d3c5ce617debf59af1bce80dfc5ba28b7","request_identity_sha256":"87d0955d6145d53775a5d627e0a19b9cbe9946d4343b617cd65107521c209d0d","reviewer_identity_sha256":"6832030d37bc6b05f4de12f913ecdea182594ad5d7ac3dcd33edcb54d7bd3a1a","role":"SIGN","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v2","structural_context_sha256":"ec8cc86da9d81ce8a38b5be410cca5062f602d489d08646f9fd3ed8657b0909d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-005","SRC-039"],"review_text":"The work addresses the fundamental challenge of learning efficient document representations, a core problem in natural language processing and machine learning. By proposing Doc2VecC, which decouples model complexity from corpus size and relies on simple averaging of word embeddings, the paper introduces a paradigm that is highly scalable and computationally lightweight. This approach is likely to influence multiple research areas by providing a robust, low-cost alternative to more complex architectures like Paragraph Vectors or Skip-thought vectors, particularly for applications where training and inference efficiency are critical constraints.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-BRD"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-021","SRC-033","SRC-036"],"review_text":"In the domain of text understanding, Doc2VecC demonstrates strong performance on sentiment analysis, document classification, and semantic relatedness tasks. The method effectively addresses the challenge of sparsity and high dimensionality inherent in bag-of-words models while avoiding the parameter explosion associated with Paragraph Vectors. The paper shows that Doc2VecC produces well-clustered representations for document classification (as visualized in t-SNE plots) and achieves competitive results on the SICK dataset, indicating its utility for practitioners seeking efficient document embedding solutions in specialized fields such as information retrieval and text classification.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-DOM"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-023","SRC-027","SRC-032","SRC-038"],"review_text":"Doc2VecC matches or outperforms state-of-the-art methods in several key aspects. On the IMDB sentiment analysis task, it achieves error rates comparable to or better than Paragraph Vectors and significantly better than Bag-of-Words. In document classification on the Wikipedia dataset, it outperforms all baselines by a significant margin across various embedding dimensions. While it trails behind LSTM-based methods on the SICK semantic relatedness task, it significantly outperforms Skip-thought vectors on the IMDB dataset and offers a substantial efficiency advantage, training in less than 2 hours on a CPU compared to 2 weeks on a GPU for Skip-thought vectors. The improvements in efficiency are particularly notable, with testing time reduced to 7 seconds compared to 4 minutes and 17 seconds for Paragraph Vectors.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-SOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-027","SRC-029","SRC-039"],"review_text":"The practical impact of Doc2VecC is significant due to its computational efficiency. The ability to train on a standard desktop CPU and generate document representations in seconds makes it accessible for large-scale applications where GPU resources may be limited or expensive. The data-dependent regularization mechanism, which suppresses common but uninformative words, enhances the interpretability and quality of the learned representations. This efficiency and robustness have potential societal benefits by enabling more widespread deployment of NLP technologies in resource-constrained environments, although the paper does not explicitly discuss broader societal risks or fairness considerations.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"179411569b035f9fb5021cadbebf171f1e447a0d8cb81de32438bb3c6aa4b40c","paper_id":"B1Igu2ogg","paper_ordinal":7,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"016086e204a01334fa8a3fad7a05be3d3c5ce617debf59af1bce80dfc5ba28b7","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"B1Igu2ogg","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"a602b1c44815e217716fb8b90687175ebebe53d7701cdfbe465560fc42a6f164","request_identity_sha256":"87d0955d6145d53775a5d627e0a19b9cbe9946d4343b617cd65107521c209d0d","role":"SIGN","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v2","usage":{"completion_tokens":865,"prompt_tokens":19476,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":20341},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"87d0955d6145d53775a5d627e0a19b9cbe9946d4343b617cd65107521c209d0d","role":"SIGN","role_ordinal":2,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v1"}